WEBVTT

00:09.567 --> 00:10.367
Hi there.

00:10.367 --> 00:12.655
Welcome to this video
where we are going to learn

00:12.655 --> 00:16.015
about digital systems
and the digital environment.

00:16.415 --> 00:20.367
The goal of the video is to help
you understand what a digital environment is,

00:20.367 --> 00:23.487
and what the building blocks
of digital systems are.

00:24.207 --> 00:28.767
In the video, firstly, we will
look at what we mean by digital devices.

00:29.055 --> 00:33.215
Following this, we will explore
what we mean by a digital environment.

00:33.567 --> 00:36.447
Finally, we will take a look
at what the building blocks

00:36.447 --> 00:39.455
of digital systems are.

00:43.503 --> 00:44.911
People in today's world

00:44.911 --> 00:47.903
spend a lot of time using digital devices.

00:48.351 --> 00:51.711
Computers, smartphones
and tablets are examples

00:51.711 --> 00:55.743
of digital devices that make up
the digital environment around us.

00:56.143 --> 00:59.231
Digital devices
help us with work and school

00:59.231 --> 01:02.223
as well as with family
and leisure activities.

01:02.271 --> 01:05.311
People work online with their
peers on the same project.

01:05.311 --> 01:09.311
We can go online to pay bills
or apartment rent, and we can watch TV

01:09.311 --> 01:12.911
shows and buy tickets
to a sports event on our digital devices.

01:13.343 --> 01:16.191
People also use
various application programs,

01:16.191 --> 01:19.423
commonly called apps,
to study and communicate.

01:19.743 --> 01:22.943
We send messages and photos
using messaging apps.

01:23.311 --> 01:27.951
People can play games on their devices
alone or with friends who are far away.

01:28.383 --> 01:32.975
In short, most of us cannot
imagine our lives without digital devices.

01:36.735 --> 01:37.935
Not all of the digital devices

01:37.935 --> 01:41.263
we use are a part
of the digital environment.

01:41.695 --> 01:44.287
A digital environment is any environment

01:44.287 --> 01:47.295
where your digital device
is connected to the internet.

01:48.591 --> 01:51.231
Typically, a food mixer
and a vacuum cleaner

01:51.231 --> 01:54.223
are non-digital electric home appliances.

01:54.303 --> 01:58.223
Some digital home appliances
have mini computers inside them.

01:58.511 --> 02:03.311
For example, a washing machine has a mini
computer to manage washing programs.

02:03.711 --> 02:07.983
Such devices can sometimes be updated
using special tools that connect

02:07.983 --> 02:12.671
to the appliance using another connection
type, for example Bluetooth.

02:13.311 --> 02:16.703
Not all of these appliances
are connected to the internet.

02:17.071 --> 02:20.031
However, a refrigerator
with a wireless internet connection

02:20.031 --> 02:23.183
is part of the digital environment.

02:23.951 --> 02:27.903
Owners could use mobile
or web applications to check humidity,

02:27.983 --> 02:30.991
temperature, or appliance status data.

02:31.583 --> 02:35.551
Digital devices also include
computers and smartphones.

02:36.031 --> 02:38.591
All digital devices and internet connected

02:38.591 --> 02:41.950
appliances make up
what we call a personal network.

02:43.470 --> 02:46.302
What devices are part
of your personal network?

02:46.302 --> 02:49.310
How do these digital devices work?

02:52.462 --> 02:53.422
Digital systems

02:53.422 --> 02:57.422
help our digital devices to work,
and these systems are built with computer

02:57.422 --> 03:00.830
programs and applications
that are called software.

03:01.422 --> 03:06.382
Software is a broad term that includes
games, online educational systems,

03:06.430 --> 03:11.102
text editing tools, and booking systems
to buy tickets or rent apartments.

03:11.342 --> 03:14.350
Software can be standalone or remote.

03:14.654 --> 03:18.286
Standalone software is installed
on the user's personal device.

03:18.526 --> 03:22.606
For example, personal digital devices
have operating system software

03:22.606 --> 03:26.366
which enables all of the devices,
functions, and controls

03:26.366 --> 03:30.798
the installation of applications
such as games or a work related program.

03:31.246 --> 03:32.686
The installed applications

03:32.686 --> 03:36.206
use the computing resources
and settings of the personal device.

03:36.686 --> 03:40.766
You may have noticed that older devices
have fewer computing resources.

03:41.166 --> 03:44.286
For example,
maybe you have an old computer, phone,

03:44.286 --> 03:49.278
or gaming system that cannot run new games
that require more computing resources.

03:53.358 --> 03:54.638
In comparison,

03:54.638 --> 03:58.430
other computer programs and applications
are connected to the internet,

03:58.446 --> 04:02.318
and these online systems
run on remote computers.

04:02.670 --> 04:06.350
These remote computers
are located somewhere else,

04:06.350 --> 04:08.158
often far away from the user.

04:08.158 --> 04:11.358
Access to online systems
happens thanks to software

04:11.358 --> 04:14.366
installed locally on the personal device.

04:14.366 --> 04:18.766
In most cases, people need browsers
to access online systems.

04:18.926 --> 04:22.046
We can think of local
software programs as opening

04:22.046 --> 04:25.054
a portal to powerful online resources.

04:25.214 --> 04:28.206
Standalone applications can work offline.

04:28.366 --> 04:32.334
For example, some games
allow users to play without the internet.

04:32.606 --> 04:36.094
However, they can be connected
to the internet to send data

04:36.094 --> 04:40.094
or retrieve data
from to remote computers upon request.

04:40.654 --> 04:41.886
For example,

04:41.886 --> 04:45.774
the results are sent to a remote computer
when the internet is available.

04:46.126 --> 04:48.046
That way, the remote computer

04:48.046 --> 04:51.326
can make a game leaderboard
after getting the results.

04:51.806 --> 04:56.686
However, many games are only functional
with the internet, such as multiplayer

04:56.734 --> 05:00.206
games that allow several users
to play together in real time.

05:00.766 --> 05:04.446
Thus, a locally installed game
application sends data

05:04.446 --> 05:08.734
about the user's actions
to a remote computer without any delay.

05:10.078 --> 05:13.486
Which of your digital
devices connect to the internet?

05:13.486 --> 05:17.166
What applications on these devices
can be used without the internet?

05:21.597 --> 05:22.909
So in this short video,

05:22.909 --> 05:25.917
we learned that we are
part of the digital environment

05:25.917 --> 05:29.229
when we are using devices
that are connected to the internet.

05:29.677 --> 05:30.749
We have also learned

05:30.749 --> 05:35.117
That the digital systems such as
smartphones, gaming consoles and computers

05:35.117 --> 05:38.429
work because of software
that is either standalone or remote.

05:40.669 --> 05:42.237
Thank you for watching.

05:42.237 --> 05:45.181
Do not forget to watch
other videos in our series.